# Draft knowledge entry: Boost.Python OHOS smoke tests should avoid Python::Python leaking -lintl
id: DRAFT-boost-python312-ohos-python-target-intl-linkage
trigger_tool: cmake|conan|python|ld
phase: test_package|consumer-link|ci
error_signature: "boost/.*test package.*Linking CXX executable|/data/service/hnp/bin/ld: cannot find -lintl|Python::Python|Python_LIBRARY"

severity: 3
category: boost|python|cmake|linking|ohos|ci
match_keywords: Boost.Python, Python::Python, Python_LIBRARY, Python_LIBRARIES, libpython3.12.so, -lintl, gettext, OHOS

title: Boost.Python OHOS test_package should link absolute libpython when Python::Python exposes -lintl
root_cause: >
  Official OHOS CI can provide CPython 3.12 through a bundled HNP layout where CMake's
  Python::Python imported target exposes a bare -lintl link item. The target libpython path is
  known, but the linker command has no default search path containing libintl, so the smoke test
  executable fails to link even though the Boost package itself was built successfully.
affected_scope: >
  Boost.Python Conan test_package consumers on HarmonyOS PC that call FindPython and link
  Python::Python while the official CI Python installation advertises gettext/intl link flags.
verification_cmd: |
  CI_PACKAGES="archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1" CI_BRANCH="feat/boost-1.90.0.2.1" CI_PR_NUMBER="6712" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: link-discovered-python-library-directly-in-ohos-smoke
rec_description: >
  Continue using FindPython for include and artifact discovery, but for OHOS test_package links use
  the absolute Python_LIBRARY cache value supplied by the recipe. Fall back to the first
  Python_LIBRARIES entry only if Python_LIBRARY is unavailable, and keep Python::Python for
  non-OHOS hosts.
rec_command: |
  set(_boost_test_python_library Python::Python)
  if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "OHOS" OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "HarmonyOS")
    set(_boost_test_python_library "${Python_LIBRARY}")
    if(NOT _boost_test_python_library AND Python_LIBRARIES)
      list(GET Python_LIBRARIES 0 _boost_test_python_library)
    endif()
  endif()
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: ohos-test-package-direct-libpython-link

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: add-python-libdir-only-for-diagnosis
fallback_description: >
  Adding the Python installation lib directory to the link search path can diagnose why -lintl is
  unresolved, but do not add gettext/libintl as a Boost package dependency unless Boost itself
  requires it. Prefer avoiding the imported target's optional system-link interface in the smoke
  test.
fallback_command: |
  cmake --build test_package/build --verbose
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: consumer-link-diagnosis

forbid_1_pattern: "add gettext dependency to boost just for test_package -lintl|package libintl with boost"
forbid_1_reason: The failure is caused by the consumer test's Python imported target interface, not by Boost's packaged libraries.
forbid_1_consequence: The PR would mix unrelated dependency adaptation into the Boost.Python package.
forbid_2_pattern: "drop Python.h or CPython initialization from the smoke test"
forbid_2_reason: The smoke test must still prove that Boost.Python and the target CPython ABI are usable by downstream consumers.
forbid_2_consequence: eigenpy may later fail even though the dependency PR appears green.

principles: consumer-link-minimization, recipe-owned-python-discovery, no-unrelated-dependencies
causes:
caused_by: DRAFT-boost-python312-cmake-discovery
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of: eigenpy-3.13.0

